<title>JAPAN: Kyocera plans to cut trading unit to 100 shares.</title>
<headline>Kyocera plans to cut trading unit to 100 shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyocera Corp said on Tuesday that it plans to change its stock trading unit to 100 shares from 1,000 shares on February 3, 1997.</p>
<p>The move was aimed at widening the firm's range of investors, and needed official approval at a shareholder meeting scheduled for December 19, the company said in a statement.</p>
